<%# FDA's small-dispenser test, per the 2026-08-06 exemption notice. Checked 2026-11-13. %>
<p>
  For FDA&rsquo;s exemption, a pharmacy is a <strong>small dispenser</strong> if the company that owns it has a
  total of <strong>25 or fewer full-time employees</strong> who are licensed pharmacists or qualified pharmacy
  technicians, counted as of <strong><%= DscsaDeadline.qualifying_label %></strong>. Full-time follows the IRS
  test: 30 or more hours a week, or 130 a month. Qualifying pharmacies don&rsquo;t apply or file anything,
  though FDA recommends telling your trading partners that you rely on the exemption.
</p>
